The goal is to recommend optimal nightly prices for Airbnb listings by analyzing patterns in:

- Seasonality (e.g., prices are higher on weekends or holidays)

- Historical demand (e.g., occupancy trends)

- Property behavior (e.g., some listings do better in peak months)

This model will:

Help hosts set smart prices rather than guesswork or flat rates

Capture what prices worked before in similar conditions

Enable a data-driven pricing strategy that can adjust to market signals

This is crucial in Airbnb-type platforms where overpricing leads to missed bookings, and underpricing leaves money on the table.
